    "sectionId": "RS-02",
    "title": "Verifying and reporting",
    "markdown": "When a message is suspicious, agencies advise verifying through a separate, trusted channel — for example a known phone number or by typing the organisation’s address into the browser — rather than using links or contact details in the message [FTC-PHISH; CISA-PHISH].\n\nSuspected phishing should be reported through the organisation’s reporting route; early reports let security teams warn others and block the campaign [NCSC-PHISH; CISA-PHISH]. Someone who has already clicked or entered details should report immediately rather than hide it [NCSC-PHISH].",
